      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ideally, yes, but:\n\n- For the stub file generation, the build system doesn\u0027t know what files metalava would emit -- in fact, it may not any stub files if all classes are hidden, so we can\u0027t rely on them.\n\n- I don\u0027t believe there\u0027s any other output files metalava always emit *but removes when it fails*, and even if we had, we often change options to pass to metalava, so I think using a timestamp file is the most straightforward and robust way.",
